<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Feb producer/import prices up 0.2 pct vs Jan.</title>
<headline>Swiss Feb producer/import prices up 0.2 pct vs Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The combined index for Swiss producer and import prices rose 0.2 percent in February versus January, but on a year-on-year basis was 1.2 percent lower than in January 1996, the Federal Statistics Office said.</p>
<p>				    Feb 1997   Jan 1997   Feb 1996</p>
<p>Monthly pct index change    +0.2 pct   0.0	 -0.4</p>
<p>Yr/yr pct index change	-1.2	-1.9	 -2.0</p>
<p>Index (100 = May 1993)	96.8	 96.9	 98.0</p>
<p>Note - The combined producer/import price index replaced the wholesale price index in May 1993.</p>
<p>The office also detailed the producer price index:</p>
<p>				    Feb 1997   Jan 1997   Feb 1996</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change  -0.1	  0.0	 -0.5</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct index change    -1.5	 -1.9	 -1.4</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)     96.8	 96.9	 98.2</p>
<p>Import price index:</p>
<p>				    Feb 1997   Jan 1997   Feb 1996</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change   +1.0	 +0.7	-0.4</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct index change     -0.6	 -1.9	-3.4</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)	96.9	 96.0	97.5</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
